.TH CP 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
cp \- copy files and directory trees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cp
.RB [ \-iprR ]
.I source ... destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
The source file is opened for reading and copied into the destination.
Unlike V1's pairs of operands, maux accepts source ... destination:
with several sources, the destination must be a directory.
If the destination is a directory, each file is copied under its own name.
An existing destination file is replaced, not appended to.
.TP
.B \-i
Prompt before replacing an existing file; only y or Y proceeds.
.TP
.B \-p
Preserve ProDOS access, file type, auxiliary type, creation date
and modification date.
.TP
.B \-r, \-R
Copy directory trees recursively, merging into an existing destination
directory where necessary.
.PP
Without -r or -R, a directory source is refused.
Errors are reported and remaining source operands are attempted.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/CP  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
mv(1), cat(1), chmod(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 for successful or declined copies, 1 for file/copy failures, 2 for usage errors.
.SH BUGS
Replacement and recursive copying are not transactional. Keep a backup when replacing important data.
